 "open": [
  "The live apps send their full nav (plugin pages) only once Console, axHub web and AmberX are redeployed with this framework. Until then Molly shows what they already send: the nav-menu asset's items.",
  "chrome@1 still folds each app's sections into one in `mergeChrome`, so xLayout reads the raw bundle to keep the section labels. The contract is unchanged.",
  "Android twin deferred (`framework/spec/PORTING.md`).",
  "The nav-style contract was built on Opus (web-only, additive, opt-in). Under the shared rule, Opus-built foundation work gets a Fable review.",
  "Follow-the-active-page ran on every render, so whatever you closed sprang back open (the sheet's Close, and single mode inside a group). It now runs only when the page changes or its branch first appears.",
  "Collapsed width is `font size × 3.8` (it was `space × 7`, 24 px under Hub Night). The collapse rules only touch the real nav, not the settings preview. The sheet header shows the app name.",
  "Verified in the browser on the final build: collapse is on and about 49 px wide, presets swap (push), swipe down closes and swipe up opens the phone sheet, the sheet's Close works, and tapping Studio in the sheet opens it and closes Build. tsc and vite build pass."
 ]
